Package: FIESperu
Type: Package
Title: Food Insecurity Experience Scale ('FIES') Estimation for Peru
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(
    given = "Akram",
    family = "Hernández-Vásquez",
    role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "akram.hernandez.v@gmail.com",
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-1431-2526")
  )
Description: Downloads, harmonizes, and analyzes microdata from the Food
    Insecurity Module ('Módulo de Inseguridad Alimentaria') of the Peruvian
    National Household Survey ('ENAHO') conducted by the National Institute of
    Statistics and Informatics ('INEI') to estimate the prevalence of moderate
    or severe and severe food insecurity using the Food Insecurity Experience
    Scale ('FIES'). Implements the official 'INEI' weighted Rasch calibration,
    equating to the global reference standard, and combined sampling plus
    measurement error estimation under complex survey designs following
    Cafiero, Viviani, and Nord (2018) <doi:10.1016/j.measurement.2017.10.065>.
